1
00:00:01,520 --> 00:00:04,400
THIS SHOW IS CREATED
FOR ENTERTAINMENT PURPOSES ONLY

2
00:00:04,480 --> 00:00:07,080
THE CHARACTERS, BEHAVIORS
AND EVENTS ARE FICTITIOUS

3
00:00:07,160 --> 00:00:09,960
VIEWER DISCRETION IS ADVISED

4
00:02:24,080 --> 00:02:26,280
How much longer do we have to hide?

5
00:02:26,360 --> 00:02:28,040
Until they can't find you.

6
00:02:28,120 --> 00:02:30,360
<i>Intel points directly to the sniper.</i>

7
00:02:30,440 --> 00:02:33,400
To eliminate the problem at its source,
you have to kill the mastermind.

8
00:02:33,480 --> 00:02:34,680
Who are you working for?

9
00:02:34,760 --> 00:02:36,880
Hurry! Time's running out!

10
00:02:41,320 --> 00:02:42,600
<i>I found some intel</i>

11
00:02:42,680 --> 00:02:45,320
<i>on who’s backing Seehan.</i>

12
00:02:48,120 --> 00:02:49,280
<i>Kill Gun for me.</i>

13
00:03:04,520 --> 00:03:06,120
I thought poverty drove you to this…

14
00:03:08,080 --> 00:03:09,120
but no.

15
00:03:11,840 --> 00:03:14,840
Do you know what's scarier than money?

16
00:03:17,760 --> 00:03:20,480
It's people who think
this bullshit is normal.

17
00:03:21,840 --> 00:03:24,400
No wonder this world
never gets any better.

18
00:03:25,720 --> 00:03:27,280
Because people who think like you

19
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:29,240
are worse than a plague.

20
00:03:29,320 --> 00:03:30,240
Hey.

21
00:03:32,720 --> 00:03:34,360
Calm down, Gun.

22
00:03:40,440 --> 00:03:43,120
If you want to kill Seehan
to avenge your grandma,

23
00:03:44,360 --> 00:03:45,320
come.

24
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:49,600
I’ll help you.

25
00:03:54,240 --> 00:03:57,400
It must be delicious, sir,
seeing how much you're eating.

26
00:03:58,440 --> 00:03:59,680
Very delicious.

27
00:04:00,360 --> 00:04:04,080
I have to say, full stomach,
but the wallet is still intact.

28
00:04:05,800 --> 00:04:09,200
I think you misspoke, sir.
We should say, full stomach,

29
00:04:09,280 --> 00:04:11,000
and getting even more money.

30
00:04:13,760 --> 00:04:15,720
Yes, yes! Absolutely right.

31
00:04:16,920 --> 00:04:18,040
Here.

32
00:04:18,120 --> 00:04:19,320
Let's have another toast.

33
00:06:31,360 --> 00:06:33,280
I hope you enjoyed the meal today, sir.

34
00:06:34,400 --> 00:06:36,400
Very much. By the way,

35
00:06:37,080 --> 00:06:39,680
what stroke of luck did you have today?

36
00:06:40,720 --> 00:06:43,000
Giving all of us
such massive bonuses like this.

37
00:06:44,040 --> 00:06:48,440
I'm not the only lucky one.
It's a win for all three of us.

38
00:06:48,520 --> 00:06:53,240
We're celebrating a business opportunity
with no enemies and no competitors.

39
00:06:53,320 --> 00:06:54,600
Just think about it.

40
00:06:55,120 --> 00:06:58,840
Our business is going
to be incredibly prosperous.

41
00:07:13,200 --> 00:07:16,440
BOSS HOTEL

42
00:07:54,120 --> 00:07:57,000
You look tired today.

43
00:07:59,560 --> 00:08:01,880
I'll get some warm water for you.

44
00:08:02,680 --> 00:08:04,000
Can I trust you?

45
00:08:12,280 --> 00:08:14,360
I want to know if I can trust you.

46
00:08:16,320 --> 00:08:17,440
Answer me.

47
00:08:19,680 --> 00:08:22,000
I don't know what you just went through,

48
00:08:23,440 --> 00:08:25,240
but if you don't trust me,

49
00:08:25,840 --> 00:08:30,440
you can leave me anywhere.
I want to go back to where I belong too.

50
00:08:31,920 --> 00:08:36,559
I'm all alone anyway.
If I die, it means nothing.

51
00:08:38,760 --> 00:08:40,640
I only have one regret.

52
00:08:41,240 --> 00:08:44,240
I set out to be a nurse, to help people.

53
00:08:44,320 --> 00:08:47,960
But if this is where my good karma
runs out, then let's get it over with.

54
00:09:08,040 --> 00:09:10,400
You don't have to worry. I keep my word.

55
00:09:10,480 --> 00:09:12,320
I'll keep your secret.

56
00:09:12,400 --> 00:09:15,240
I won't give a statement to the police.
I won't tell anyone.

57
00:09:15,760 --> 00:09:19,960
But if you still don't trust me,
and you're afraid of the fallout,

58
00:09:20,040 --> 00:09:21,640
just kill me.

59
00:09:22,520 --> 00:09:25,520
If I die, your story stays a secret.

60
00:10:00,160 --> 00:10:01,240
I'm sorry…

61
00:10:08,080 --> 00:10:09,880
for putting you through all this.

62
00:10:19,640 --> 00:10:21,040
I'll take care of you myself.

63
00:10:31,600 --> 00:10:34,400
You knew Gun was waiting to kill you,
yet you still called us in.

64
00:10:35,040 --> 00:10:37,320
Sir, I am truly sorry.

65
00:10:37,960 --> 00:10:42,480
The thing is, I actually wanted
to set a trap to kill him.

66
00:10:42,560 --> 00:10:44,720
But your plan fell apart.

67
00:10:45,360 --> 00:10:48,400
All of us were almost doomed
because of you.

68
00:10:49,920 --> 00:10:51,920
I'm truly sorry. I apologize once again.

69
00:10:52,520 --> 00:10:56,440
I promise I'll get this sorted out.

70
00:10:57,040 --> 00:10:58,120
You don't have to.

71
00:10:59,520 --> 00:11:03,360
Paisan, use the law to crush him.

72
00:11:03,440 --> 00:11:07,280
How can I do that?
How could I step on Decha's toes?

73
00:11:07,960 --> 00:11:11,920
He was a subordinate in his chain
of command. Let him handle it himself.

74
00:11:13,360 --> 00:11:17,000
Don't make me stick my neck out yet.
I have to clean up his mess first.

75
00:11:18,120 --> 00:11:20,880
Just hiring Gun and Han

76
00:11:20,960 --> 00:11:24,080
is enough to get the committee
breathing down my neck.

77
00:11:27,200 --> 00:11:28,800
But if you close this case,

78
00:11:30,200 --> 00:11:31,920
you will get all the credit.

79
00:11:34,880 --> 00:11:37,040
And I'll put you forward for a promotion.

80
00:11:56,800 --> 00:11:58,160
We've located Gun, sir.

81
00:12:31,360 --> 00:12:32,440
It's me.

82
00:13:04,440 --> 00:13:05,480
I think we're safe now.

83
00:13:13,200 --> 00:13:14,120
Go. Go!

84
00:13:16,400 --> 00:13:17,520
We found Gun.

85
00:13:25,040 --> 00:13:26,040
Stop right there, Gun.

86
00:13:27,600 --> 00:13:28,680
Drop the gun.

87
00:13:33,600 --> 00:13:34,440
I said drop it!

88
00:13:37,160 --> 00:13:38,000
Follow my lead.

89
00:13:39,800 --> 00:13:43,800
Help! Help me! Please help me!

90
00:13:43,880 --> 00:13:45,200
Play along.

91
00:13:45,280 --> 00:13:48,280
Help!

92
00:13:48,360 --> 00:13:50,600
Back off! Or I'll shoot.

93
00:13:51,480 --> 00:13:53,720
Help. Help!

94
00:13:55,960 --> 00:13:57,240
I said back off!

95
00:14:10,760 --> 00:14:12,440
The suspect took a woman hostage, sir.

96
00:14:13,160 --> 00:14:14,160
Back off!

97
00:14:15,360 --> 00:14:16,400
What should we do, sir?

98
00:14:18,480 --> 00:14:19,560
Shoot to kill.

99
00:14:29,720 --> 00:14:32,800
You would shoot even with a hostage here?

100
00:14:33,520 --> 00:14:34,640
I don't care.

101
00:15:20,960 --> 00:15:23,040
Rada, only pack what's necessary.

102
00:15:35,240 --> 00:15:38,200
<i>Chaos erupted</i>
<i>during a hostage rescue operation</i>

103
00:15:38,280 --> 00:15:42,960
<i>when the suspect shot a gas cylinder,</i>
<i>causing a massive explosion,</i>

104
00:15:43,040 --> 00:15:45,200
<i>before using the chaos to escape…</i>

105
00:15:45,800 --> 00:15:48,000
Gun is incredibly skilled.

106
00:15:49,960 --> 00:15:52,400
Honestly, I don't want to kill him.

107
00:15:53,720 --> 00:15:56,600
If I could get him to work for me,

108
00:15:57,360 --> 00:15:59,160
it would be far more beneficial.

109
00:16:02,160 --> 00:16:05,600
His crimes are piling up.
The police won't let him off, sir.

110
00:16:06,120 --> 00:16:08,960
SUSPECT TRIGGERS GAS EXPLOSION
GENERAL PAISAN'S UNIT FAILS ARREST

111
00:16:11,800 --> 00:16:15,880
This bastard's got a big ego too.
He can't stand losing face.

112
00:16:48,800 --> 00:16:50,480
We'll stay here for now.

113
00:16:51,960 --> 00:16:53,760
How much longer will we be here?

114
00:16:54,600 --> 00:16:55,880
Until there's no need to run.

115
00:17:21,560 --> 00:17:23,720
Don't go out unless you really need to.

116
00:17:24,920 --> 00:17:26,560
I could go out there to help you.

117
00:17:40,600 --> 00:17:45,200
Hey, what kind of trouble are you in?
Why do you have to kill people?

118
00:17:51,800 --> 00:17:54,400
You don't have to answer me.

119
00:18:05,520 --> 00:18:07,040
If stopping them were easy,

120
00:18:10,760 --> 00:18:12,160
people wouldn't have to die.

121
00:18:20,440 --> 00:18:24,520
Even Paisan couldn't catch Gun.
I think he must have had help.

122
00:18:25,280 --> 00:18:26,280
Yes.

123
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:29,640
He wouldn't have survived
this long working alone.

124
00:18:39,520 --> 00:18:40,840
Hey.

125
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:43,280
Are you thinking it's me?

126
00:18:43,360 --> 00:18:45,560
Huh? No.

127
00:18:47,600 --> 00:18:48,480
Or is it you?

128
00:18:52,480 --> 00:18:55,720
Even though I knew Gun
during our training,

129
00:18:55,800 --> 00:18:57,240
I know where to draw the line.

130
00:19:00,680 --> 00:19:04,360
His ideology and mine are polar opposites.

131
00:19:05,120 --> 00:19:07,480
If everyone chose guns over the law,

132
00:19:08,400 --> 00:19:10,360
the country would go to complete shit.

133
00:19:12,800 --> 00:19:14,080
I still believe in the system.

134
00:19:21,160 --> 00:19:24,160
So, who do you think is helping Gun?

135
00:19:28,960 --> 00:19:30,680
I'd like to know that myself.

136
00:19:59,200 --> 00:20:00,880
I didn't order anything.

137
00:20:51,840 --> 00:20:53,840
You already knew it was me,

138
00:20:55,080 --> 00:20:56,960
yet you still pulled a gun on me.

139
00:21:21,800 --> 00:21:24,640
What were you thinking,
bringing her with you?

140
00:21:27,960 --> 00:21:31,680
If I let her go, she'd be dead.

141
00:21:32,600 --> 00:21:34,920
You know women are dangerous.

142
00:21:35,880 --> 00:21:38,880
They're a secret weapon
used to kill many top-tier assassins.

143
00:21:39,760 --> 00:21:41,440
But forget about assassins.

144
00:21:42,680 --> 00:21:44,640
Every man has fallen victim
to his own wife.

145
00:21:46,920 --> 00:21:48,200
What info did you get?

146
00:21:53,160 --> 00:21:56,600
Everyone you saw that day
is in cahoots with Seehan.

147
00:21:58,600 --> 00:22:00,040
Paisan is on that side too.

148
00:22:01,320 --> 00:22:05,240
To infiltrate the police force,
someone had to pave the way.

149
00:22:07,320 --> 00:22:11,200
To become this powerful,
Seehan must have connections everywhere.

150
00:22:13,200 --> 00:22:14,280
Gun.

151
00:22:17,120 --> 00:22:19,800
I'm going to resign to help you.
I can't take it anymore.

152
00:22:20,760 --> 00:22:21,840
No need.

153
00:22:22,440 --> 00:22:25,480
You stay right where you are.
I need an inside man.

154
00:22:26,280 --> 00:22:28,480
So, what are you going to do next?

155
00:22:29,200 --> 00:22:31,000
Kill Seehan and everything ends.

156
00:22:32,400 --> 00:22:34,120
Seehan isn't my target yet.

157
00:22:41,080 --> 00:22:43,640
We're no longer commander and soldier.

158
00:22:45,280 --> 00:22:48,760
You would shoot even with a hostage here?

159
00:22:49,440 --> 00:22:50,640
I don't care.

160
00:22:51,960 --> 00:22:56,120
I need to cut off his limbs first
so he can't get back up.

161
00:22:57,080 --> 00:22:58,760
Then Paisan will come down on you hard.

162
00:23:01,520 --> 00:23:03,520
I still believe
there are good cops out there.

163
00:23:05,840 --> 00:23:09,640
The lower-ranking cops
who chose this path for justice

164
00:23:09,720 --> 00:23:10,840
but can't speak up.

165
00:23:12,560 --> 00:23:16,840
As long as they're forced
to choose loyalty over integrity

166
00:23:16,920 --> 00:23:19,200
and silence over accountability,

167
00:23:20,200 --> 00:23:23,120
these ordinary cops will be on our side.

168
00:23:28,920 --> 00:23:30,000
Now I know

169
00:23:30,960 --> 00:23:32,720
where to get the info.

170
00:23:34,560 --> 00:23:36,720
You get me Paisan's dirty laundry.

171
00:23:37,840 --> 00:23:39,120
I'll handle the rest.

172
00:24:00,200 --> 00:24:03,720
You know a guy like you
shouldn't have weaknesses, right?

173
00:24:45,200 --> 00:24:48,160
METHEE: YOU GOT ANY DIRT ON PAISAN?

174
00:24:48,240 --> 00:24:50,160
AEK: WHAT KIND OF DIRT?

175
00:24:51,480 --> 00:24:52,800
METHEE: WHATEVER YOU HAVE

176
00:24:52,880 --> 00:24:56,400
AEK: ARE YOU SERIOUSLY GOING AFTER HIM?

177
00:25:06,480 --> 00:25:13,280
METHEE: ONE MESSAGE

178
00:25:13,880 --> 00:25:17,080
METHEE: I GOT THE INFO ON PAISAN

179
00:25:30,200 --> 00:25:33,160
FOR THE PUBLIC

180
00:25:33,240 --> 00:25:34,160
Hey, Aut.

181
00:25:34,680 --> 00:25:35,840
Call a team meeting, now.

182
00:25:37,200 --> 00:25:38,160
Yes, sir.

183
00:25:44,080 --> 00:25:46,040
I want you to forward it to the press too.

184
00:25:46,560 --> 00:25:48,000
GUN

185
00:25:59,200 --> 00:26:00,240
Done.

186
00:26:02,480 --> 00:26:04,960
Are you trying to shake up
the whole bureau?

187
00:26:05,720 --> 00:26:08,480
If we give him time,
he'll get off the hook again.

188
00:26:09,520 --> 00:26:11,960
Isn't that Paisan with Robert,
the gambling site owner?

189
00:26:12,920 --> 00:26:15,760
If this gets leaked,
headquarters is going to be rocked.

190
00:26:16,720 --> 00:26:19,320
-Check if this is AI generated.
-Right.

191
00:26:19,920 --> 00:26:22,880
Hurry and verify it
before this photo reaches the press.

192
00:26:22,960 --> 00:26:24,000
Yes, sir.

193
00:26:28,600 --> 00:26:31,240
Who the hell leaked these photos? Huh?

194
00:26:31,760 --> 00:26:35,440
Find out who it is,
then hurry and silence the reporters.

195
00:26:44,960 --> 00:26:46,440
-Sir.
-Sir.

196
00:26:46,520 --> 00:26:49,720
Is it true you're linked to the wanted
gambling site owner who fled Thailand?

197
00:26:49,800 --> 00:26:50,800
-Is it true, sir?
-Is it?

198
00:26:50,880 --> 00:26:51,880
-Please answer.
-Please.

199
00:26:51,960 --> 00:26:53,080
The public wants to know.

200
00:26:53,160 --> 00:26:56,960
I have absolutely no involvement
with those gambling sites.

201
00:26:57,040 --> 00:27:01,120
But I admit that I have attended
parties organized by them.

202
00:27:01,200 --> 00:27:03,800
I have no close relationship

203
00:27:03,880 --> 00:27:06,680
or personal acquaintance
with them whatsoever.

204
00:27:06,760 --> 00:27:09,520
But there's a photo of you
at Robert's son's wedding.

205
00:27:09,600 --> 00:27:12,240
You played golf with him
and went to other events. Please explain.

206
00:27:12,320 --> 00:27:13,560
It's quite clear, sir.

207
00:27:13,640 --> 00:27:15,440
Is it true, sir? Please explain.

208
00:27:15,520 --> 00:27:17,720
I think this whole thing

209
00:27:17,800 --> 00:27:21,320
is just an attempt to bring me down.

210
00:27:21,400 --> 00:27:23,760
This is more likely
a targeted smear campaign.

211
00:27:23,840 --> 00:27:25,520
Do you suspect anyone behind this?

212
00:27:25,600 --> 00:27:29,600
It will have to be investigated.
I will fight this matter to the very end.

213
00:27:29,680 --> 00:27:30,680
Is it an inside job?

214
00:27:30,760 --> 00:27:33,520
Please excuse me for today.
I have urgent business.

215
00:27:33,600 --> 00:27:34,440
Thank you very much.

216
00:27:34,520 --> 00:27:35,560
Care to clarify this now?

217
00:27:35,640 --> 00:27:37,120
-Sir.
-How do you explain this, sir?

218
00:27:37,640 --> 00:27:38,480
Excuse me, sir.

219
00:27:43,480 --> 00:27:46,040
Please come with us
to address what happened.

220
00:27:46,120 --> 00:27:48,240
-Will you clarify, sir?
-Sir.

221
00:27:48,320 --> 00:27:50,760
-Would you like to?
-What really happened, sir?

222
00:27:50,840 --> 00:27:52,600
In addition to the photos in the news,

223
00:27:52,680 --> 00:27:55,080
a money trail linked
to gambling sites was found.

224
00:27:55,160 --> 00:27:57,000
Does that mean
you are really involved, sir?

225
00:27:57,080 --> 00:27:58,000
Is it true, sir?

226
00:27:58,520 --> 00:28:00,880
-Sir.
-Sir, could you please clarify?

227
00:28:00,960 --> 00:28:02,640
Do you have a court warrant?

228
00:28:03,520 --> 00:28:05,320
I'm only asking you to clarify.

229
00:28:06,360 --> 00:28:08,760
But if you want a warrant,
that wouldn't be a problem.

230
00:28:08,840 --> 00:28:10,800
Does this mean you are involved?

231
00:28:10,880 --> 00:28:12,240
-Are you actually guilty?
-Are you?

232
00:28:12,320 --> 00:28:13,400
Do you want to clarify

233
00:28:13,480 --> 00:28:14,960
the truth about this, sir?

234
00:28:15,040 --> 00:28:17,280
-Could you please answer us?
-Sir.

235
00:28:17,360 --> 00:28:21,520
<i>The Royal Thai Police has formed</i>
<i>an urgent investigative panel</i>

236
00:28:21,600 --> 00:28:25,320
<i>and temporarily suspended</i>
<i>Police Major General Paisan from his post.</i>

237
00:28:38,480 --> 00:28:39,880
He's been arrested.

238
00:28:39,960 --> 00:28:42,480
But someone of his status
won't have trouble getting bail.

239
00:28:42,560 --> 00:28:46,080
The evidence pinning him down
is solid. Plus,

240
00:28:47,040 --> 00:28:48,720
people are lined up to take his spot.

241
00:28:48,800 --> 00:28:51,000
They won't let him get bail easily.

242
00:28:52,520 --> 00:28:53,840
They want him behind bars.

243
00:28:54,960 --> 00:28:57,680
He'll probably try everything
to avoid prison.

244
00:28:57,760 --> 00:28:59,480
That's exactly what I want.

245
00:29:02,600 --> 00:29:04,160
What are you planning to do?

246
00:29:08,480 --> 00:29:11,320
I'm sorry. I didn't mean to eavesdrop,

247
00:29:11,400 --> 00:29:13,080
but that day, I overheard

248
00:29:13,160 --> 00:29:16,400
you and your friend planning
to deal with him.

249
00:29:17,920 --> 00:29:21,000
Are you going to kill him?

250
00:29:25,080 --> 00:29:26,320
If he died,

251
00:29:27,920 --> 00:29:29,200
it'd be a waste.

252
00:29:59,840 --> 00:30:00,840
Hey.

253
00:30:01,480 --> 00:30:02,560
I got the info.

254
00:30:03,680 --> 00:30:05,760
While drafting the case for prosecutors,

255
00:30:06,640 --> 00:30:08,680
where are the police holding Paisan?

256
00:30:10,840 --> 00:30:12,800
There are still plenty of good cops left.

257
00:30:16,200 --> 00:30:17,560
They sent me the location.

258
00:30:37,000 --> 00:30:38,760
Go silence him.

259
00:30:39,800 --> 00:30:42,240
Boss, you want me to kill General Paisan?

260
00:30:43,280 --> 00:30:44,760
I know his true nature well.

261
00:30:46,280 --> 00:30:47,880
He is an expert at begging

262
00:30:48,520 --> 00:30:50,400
and bargaining.

263
00:30:51,760 --> 00:30:53,560
When he's cornered,

264
00:30:54,400 --> 00:30:56,040
he knows how to save his own skin.

265
00:30:57,600 --> 00:30:59,800
He takes all the credit
and shifts the blame.

266
00:31:05,160 --> 00:31:06,600
Go find out

267
00:31:07,840 --> 00:31:09,840
where he's being locked up.

268
00:31:10,440 --> 00:31:11,480
Yes, Boss.

269
00:32:03,480 --> 00:32:06,720
Sir, do you think Gun will make a move?

270
00:32:08,160 --> 00:32:11,760
He sent me dirt on Paisan.
That means he must have a plan.

271
00:32:11,840 --> 00:32:13,400
What do you think he's up to?

272
00:32:14,520 --> 00:32:18,600
He knows that during his trial,
Paisan will be kept in custody.

273
00:32:19,480 --> 00:32:23,560
This is his only chance to take Paisan out
before he's sent to prison. It's easier.

274
00:32:23,640 --> 00:32:25,280
So what should we do?

275
00:32:25,360 --> 00:32:26,440
What can we do?

276
00:32:27,400 --> 00:32:29,720
Just don't be careless. Go patrol.

277
00:32:29,800 --> 00:32:30,840
Yes, sir.

278
00:33:04,720 --> 00:33:07,800
How is it going? Anything suspicious?

279
00:33:07,880 --> 00:33:09,520
None, sir. Everything is in order.

280
00:33:59,040 --> 00:34:00,160
You can't enter.

281
00:34:24,480 --> 00:34:26,560
Hey! Hey!

282
00:35:50,440 --> 00:35:52,160
You broke in here. What do you want?

283
00:35:52,960 --> 00:35:56,560
I want to see a scumbag like you
face the consequences of what you've done.

284
00:35:59,440 --> 00:36:00,600
Do you even realize…

285
00:36:02,520 --> 00:36:04,880
that the poor you've trampled on

286
00:36:05,960 --> 00:36:08,480
never even had a chance
to beg for their lives?

287
00:36:09,960 --> 00:36:11,600
But you have everything.

288
00:36:11,680 --> 00:36:14,640
Power, the police, the law.

289
00:36:15,600 --> 00:36:19,000
Yet you still choose to be their lapdog.

290
00:36:24,720 --> 00:36:27,080
You think you are any better than me?

291
00:36:27,160 --> 00:36:29,600
Hell no, you bastard. I'm no hero.

292
00:36:29,680 --> 00:36:31,480
I pick the right target. A guy like you!

293
00:36:36,440 --> 00:36:38,200
Those people are not above the law.

294
00:36:41,000 --> 00:36:43,000
But they buy off law enforcers like you.

295
00:36:45,880 --> 00:36:47,080
So what do you want from me?

296
00:36:51,920 --> 00:36:53,200
The truth.

297
00:36:54,920 --> 00:36:58,240
You choose. Will you speak as a cop…

298
00:37:00,880 --> 00:37:02,480
or as their lapdog?

299
00:37:21,680 --> 00:37:24,480
I want the list of everyone higher up.

300
00:37:26,960 --> 00:37:28,160
The ones giving the orders,

301
00:37:30,000 --> 00:37:31,360
the ones paying,

302
00:37:32,600 --> 00:37:34,040
the ones laundering the money,

303
00:37:35,800 --> 00:37:38,280
and the ones poisoning this country.

304
00:37:42,920 --> 00:37:45,200
You know full well
that if I talk, I'm dead.

305
00:37:45,280 --> 00:37:47,000
But if you don't talk,

306
00:37:47,080 --> 00:37:48,880
you'll die right now.

307
00:37:53,880 --> 00:37:57,680
If you talk, I'll give you a chance

308
00:37:59,160 --> 00:38:00,320
to survive.

309
00:38:39,280 --> 00:38:42,880
Gun's the only one who might know
who's pulling all the strings.

310
00:38:42,960 --> 00:38:44,040
Where should we begin?

311
00:38:44,120 --> 00:38:46,000
<i>I forgot about someone close to Gun.</i>

312
00:38:48,800 --> 00:38:50,400
<i>Why do you want a cactus?</i>

313
00:38:50,480 --> 00:38:55,040
It's just like me.
It doesn't need much care to grow.

314
00:38:55,120 --> 00:38:57,360
All it needs is a little light.

315
00:38:57,440 --> 00:39:00,800
We're working together,
so we expect a bigger return.

316
00:39:01,480 --> 00:39:03,560
Submit a proposal
to open the border for me.

317
00:39:03,640 --> 00:39:06,200
They will sign the papers
to launch the border project.

318
00:39:06,280 --> 00:39:08,520
<i>If it gets signed,</i>
<i>there's no way to block scammers.</i>

319
00:39:08,600 --> 00:39:09,880
25TH ANNIVERSARY: MODEL CITIZEN

320
00:39:13,160 --> 00:39:15,680
Cut four, take one. Take two.

321
00:39:31,920 --> 00:39:32,880
Too fast.

322
00:39:54,160 --> 00:39:55,040
Take.

323
00:39:55,120 --> 00:39:56,760
And I go bam!

324
00:39:56,840 --> 00:39:59,080
-Bam, block it.
-Then I pull your leg.

325
00:39:59,160 --> 00:40:00,960
I drop and do an overhead kick.

326
00:40:01,040 --> 00:40:02,120
-Bam!
-I pull again.

327
00:40:02,200 --> 00:40:05,160
-Drop down again, and punch. Bam!
-Bam!

328
00:40:05,240 --> 00:40:07,840
-Then I catch.
-Bam! I hit you and grab your neck.

329
00:40:07,920 --> 00:40:09,360
-Not that hard.
-Wow.

330
00:40:09,440 --> 00:40:10,760
Not that hard.

331
00:40:11,960 --> 00:40:12,920
Let me dab your face.

332
00:40:13,000 --> 00:40:13,920
Not that hard?

333
00:40:42,040 --> 00:40:46,360
Subtitle translation by: Anan Pratchayakul
